<title>USA: Ohio spent $928 mln on road plans in fiscal 1997.</title>
<headline>Ohio spent $928 mln on road plans in fiscal 1997.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ohio Department of Transportation invested more than $928 million on construction and maintenance in fiscal 1997, the department reported.</p>
<p>Spending increased 6 percent over fiscal 1996 and reflected the second time in the last three years that the department's spending exceeded $925 million, the department reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>The department spending included road resurfacing, bridges repairs, new construction and local government projects.</p>
<p>((--David Bailey, Chicago Newsroom, 312-408-8647))</p>
